WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.729 --> 00:00:20.414
Swallow, little Swallow," said the Prince, "will you not stay with me for one night and be my

2
00:00:20.494 --> 00:00:26.438
messenger? The boy is so thirsty, and the mother so sad."

3
00:00:26.458 --> 00:00:30.221
"I don't think I like boys," answered the Swallow.

4
00:00:30.241 --> 00:00:37.865
"Last summer, when I was staying on the river, there were two rude boys, the miller's sons, who

5
00:00:37.885 --> 00:00:39.866
were always throwing stones at me.

6
00:00:40.766 --> 00:00:47.850
They never hit me, of course; we swallows fly far too well for that, and besides, I come

7
00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:49.931
of a family famous for its agility.

8
00:00:50.612 --> 00:00:53.333
But still, it was a mark of disrespect."

9
00:00:53.873 --> 00:00:58.396
But the Happy Prince looked so sad that the little Swallow was sorry.

10
00:00:59.284 --> 00:01:05.349
"It is very cold here," he said, "but I will stay with you for one night and be

11
00:01:05.389 --> 00:01:06.250
your messenger."

12
00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:11.255
"Thank you, little Swallow," said the Prince.

13
00:01:12.315 --> 00:01:18.100
So the Swallow picked out the great ruby from the Prince's sword and flew away with it in

14
00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.382
his beak over the roofs of the town.

15
00:01:21.203 --> 00:01:26.568
He passed by the cathedral tower, where the white marble angels were sculptured.

16
00:01:27.244 --> 00:01:30.766
He passed by the palace and heard the sound of dancing.

17
00:01:31.487 --> 00:01:34.689
A beautiful girl came out on the balcony with her lover.

18
00:01:34.709 --> 00:01:42.454
"How wonderful the stars are," he said to her, "and how wonderful is the power of love!"

19
00:01:43.335 --> 00:01:47.318
"I hope my dress will be ready in time for the State Ball," she answered.

20
00:01:47.338 --> 00:01:54.182
"I have ordered passionflowers to be embroidered on it; but the seamstresses are so lazy."

21
00:01:55.043 --> 00:02:00.486
He passed over the river, and saw the lanterns hanging to the masts of the ships.

22
00:02:01.147 --> 00:02:07.270
He passed over the market, and saw the old men bargaining with each other and weighing out money

23
00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:08.531
in copper scales.

24
00:02:09.652 --> 00:02:13.674
At last, he came to the poor house and looked in.

25
00:02:14.595 --> 00:02:21.919
The boy was tossing feverishly on his bed, and the mother had fallen asleep, she was so tired.

26
00:02:22.739 --> 00:02:27.982
In he hopped, and laid the great ruby on the table beside the woman's thimble.

27
00:02:28.802 --> 00:02:34.484
Then, he flew gently round the bed, fanning the boy's forehead with his wings.

28
00:02:35.225 --> 00:02:38.186
"How cool I feel," said the boy.

29
00:02:38.206 --> 00:02:43.868
"I must be getting better," and he sank into a delicious slumber.

30
00:02:44.629 --> 00:02:49.971
Then, the Swallow flew back to the Happy Prince and told him what he had done.

31
00:02:49.991 --> 00:02:57.334
"It is curious," he remarked, "but I feel quite warm now, although it is so cold."

32
00:02:57.354 --> 00:03:02.376
"That is because you have done a good action," said the Prince.

33
00:03:03.177 --> 00:03:08.079
And the little Swallow began to think, and then, he fell asleep.

34
00:03:09.159 --> 00:03:11.420
Thinking always made him sleepy.

35
00:03:12.141 --> 00:03:15.822
When day broke, he flew down to the river and had a bath.

36
00:03:15.842 --> 00:03:23.542
"What a remarkable phenomenon," said the Professor of Ornithology as he was passing over the bridge.

37
00:03:23.562 --> 00:03:25.923
"A swallow in winter!"

38
00:03:26.383 --> 00:03:29.504
And he wrote a long letter about it to the local newspaper.

39
00:03:30.324 --> 00:03:35.887
Everyone quoted it, it was full of so many words that they could not understand.

40
00:03:35.907 --> 00:03:42.849
"Tonight, I go to Egypt," said the Swallow, and he was in high spirits at the prospect.

41
00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:49.192
He visited all the public monuments and sat a long time on top of the church steeple.

42
00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:56.983
Wherever he went, the Sparrows chirruped, and said to each other, "What a distinguished stranger!"

43
00:03:57.663 --> 00:03:59.884
So he enjoyed himself very much.

44
00:04:00.744 --> 00:04:04.166
When the moon rose, he flew back to the Happy Prince.

45
00:04:04.186 --> 00:04:06.947
"Have you any commissions for Egypt?"

46
00:04:07.607 --> 00:04:08.107
he cried.

47
00:04:08.127 --> 00:04:10.248
"I am just starting."

48
00:04:10.929 --> 00:04:19.132
"Swallow, Swallow, little Swallow," said the Prince, "will you not stay with me one night longer?"

49
00:04:20.816 --> 00:04:24.017
"I am waited for in Egypt," answered the Swallow.

50
00:04:24.037 --> 00:04:29.499
"Tomorrow, my friends will fly up to our meeting place on the River Nile.

51
00:04:30.139 --> 00:04:36.961
The hippopotamus lies there among the cattails, and on a great granite throne sits the God Memnon.

52
00:04:37.861 --> 00:04:45.003
All night long, he watches the stars, and when the morning star shines, he utters one cry of

53
00:04:45.063 --> 00:04:47.403
joy, and then, he is silent.

54
00:04:48.264 --> 00:04:53.146
At noon, the yellow lions come down to the water's edge to drink.

55
00:04:53.867 --> 00:05:00.170
They have eyes like green jewels, and their roar is louder than the roar of the river."

56
00:05:01.011 --> 00:05:11.637
"Swallow, Swallow, little Swallow," said the Prince, "far away across the city, I see a young man in

57
00:05:11.677 --> 00:05:12.177
a garret.

58
00:05:13.038 --> 00:05:20.133
He is leaning over a desk covered with papers, and in a glass by his side, there is

59
00:05:20.193 --> 00:05:22.013
a bunch of withered violets.

60
00:05:23.074 --> 00:05:30.536
His hair is brown and crisp, and his lips are red as a pomegranate, and he has large

61
00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:32.056
and dreamy eyes.

62
00:05:33.276 --> 00:05:39.818
He is trying to finish a play for the Director of the Theatre, but he is too cold

63
00:05:39.938 --> 00:05:41.118
to write any more.

64
00:05:41.919 --> 00:05:47.200
There is no fire in the fireplace, and hunger has made him faint."

65
00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:53.442
"I will wait with you one night longer," said the Swallow, who really had a good heart.

66
00:05:53.462 --> 00:05:55.643
"Shall I take him another ruby?"

67
00:05:56.444 --> 00:06:01.206
"Alas! I have no ruby now," said the Prince.

68
00:06:01.226 --> 00:06:04.727
"My eyes are all that I have left.

69
00:06:05.307 --> 00:06:13.090
They are made of rare sapphires, which were brought out of India a thousand years ago.

70
00:06:14.011 --> 00:06:16.792
Pluck out one of them and take it to him.

71
00:06:17.696 --> 00:06:23.618
He will sell it to the jeweler and buy food and firewood, and finish his play."

72
00:06:23.638 --> 00:06:30.920
"Dear Prince," said the Swallow, "I cannot do that," and he began to weep.

73
00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:40.102
"Swallow, Swallow, little Swallow," said the Prince, "do as I command you."

74
00:06:41.102 --> 00:06:46.624
So the Swallow plucked out the Prince's eye and flew away to the student's garret.

75
00:06:47.944 --> 00:06:51.827
It was easy enough to get in, as there was a hole in the roof.

76
00:06:52.748 --> 00:06:55.590
Through this, he darted and came into the room.

77
00:06:56.431 --> 00:07:01.715
The young man had his head buried in his hands, so he did not hear the flutter of

78
00:07:01.735 --> 00:07:08.921
the bird's wings, and when he looked up, he found the beautiful sapphire lying on the withered violets.

79
00:07:10.122 --> 00:07:13.785
"I am beginning to be appreciated," he cried.

80
00:07:13.805 --> 00:07:17.108
"This is from some great admirer.

81
00:07:17.756 --> 00:07:22.497
Now I can finish my play," and he looked quite happy.

82
00:07:23.418 --> 00:07:26.838
The next day, the Swallow flew down to the harbor.

83
00:07:27.579 --> 00:07:33.400
He sat on the mast of a large vessel and watched the sailors hauling big chests out of

84
00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:34.541
the hold with ropes.

85
00:07:35.401 --> 00:07:36.821
"Heave a-hoy!"

86
00:07:37.681 --> 00:07:39.862
they shouted as each chest came up.

87
00:07:39.882 --> 00:07:42.283
"I am going to Egypt!"

88
00:07:43.283 --> 00:07:49.259
cried the Swallow, but nobody minded him, and when the moon rose, he flew back to the Happy

89
00:07:49.339 --> 00:07:53.386
Prince. "I am come to bid you good-bye," he cried.
